# `startofyear` from year 0 with offset `i64::MIN` overflows `datetime` (DS4003), and must not panic.
mode: run
skip: M2-18 (`calendar::year_range` panics on `i64::MIN` year)
---- query
from '../../../data/orders.csv'
| take 1
| project y = startofyear(startofyear(timestamp, -2023), -9223372036854775808)
---- expected
error[DS4003]: the result of `startofyear` does not fit in a `datetime`
  --> query:3:15
  |
3 | | project y = startofyear(startofyear(timestamp, -2023), -9223372036854775808)
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this overflowed
  |
  = note: datetimes and timespans are counted in microseconds and hold about ±292,000 years
